{
  "rationale": "The plant automata G1 models the robot's perception of obstacles and motion capabilities, with explicit separation of perception and action. The specification automata E1 binds perception outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforcing conservative recovery only when needed and rapid return to exploration. E2 prevents repeated backward recovery and ensures no chaining of backward actions. E3 prevents oscillation between left/right turns. E4 ensures full_rotate is only used as a last resort after repeated blockages.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate perception (sensor outcomes) and motion (actions) in the plant for clarity and modularity.",
    "Specifications bind perception to safe, progress-maximizing actions, enforce recovery discipline, and prevent unsafe or inefficient behaviors."
  ],
